#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:5
#: d2d1cbd784d342f88c4d9b50afd053a9
msgid "OEM Customization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:7
#: 1b2481a9ad9644e99aeee301c4829fac
msgid "ArduPilot provides several ways for an OEM to provide firmware on their products that has been customized to their specific system configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:9
#: c811309332a0486ea36a2e776c1f3c80
msgid "Ability to have specific defaults for parameters to match included system components, such as gimbals, or entire systems' peripherals, such as in ready-to-fly vehicles. This allows the user to \"reset to defaults\" using Mission Planner or MAVProxy in case of a problem with parameters having been accidentally changed, and only have to re-calibrate compass/IMU/and RC, at most, to be ready to fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:10
#: a201037d2e074e4da512c27b3c3a8b3a
msgid "Ability to provide Lua scripts in ROM for special functions without the end-user having to load them on the SD card. Read more about Lua scripting in ArduPilot :ref:`here<common-lua-scripts>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:11
#: 11b3c433b0744134a4bdc03f33a3b0da
msgid "Ability to change the firmware string displayed to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:12
#: e4389ebdaf824f1e930cfcae69661e19
msgid "Ability to include pictures and informational files in available free flash space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:13
#: 4a47a5de0a5840b58f7de91777dc12fa
msgid "Ability to change parameters and mark them as read-only so that users cannot change them using :ref:`APJ Tools<dev:apjtools-intro>`. (as of version 4.5 firmware, this is no longer available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:14
#: 424a962205ae4f6f9e7c2ec36f03a8de
msgid "Ability to `install a LUA script to vet parameters <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/param-lockdown.md>`__ before allowing them to be set via MAVLink."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:17
#: c2e9aeac21fe4381ba1e2c45a1b94227
msgid "Customization Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:19
#: 130d7028c89e437d9410143a55221e5f
msgid "This section assumes that the OEM has set up the build environment (:ref:`building-the-code`) and cloned the ArduPilot GitHub repo locally (:ref:`where-to-get-the-code`), to build its customized version of the firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:21
#: b495d053ea4d4ce99e2a30e319bf3d91
msgid "Create a branch with the version of firmware you wish to base the customization upon. This will usually be the current stable version. To do this for ArduPlane Stable, for example, assuming you are already in the ArduPilot directory on your PC:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:33
#: b561e64e0f524883904873e007637179
msgid "In the ``libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef`` directory, create a new subdirectory for your customized board definitions. In this example, the directory will be named ``OEM_CubeOrange`` to create a derivative for that board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:35
#: 8e73650248fc42e2a210dfca4d032f79
msgid "Create a new ``hwdef.dat`` file in this format. In this case, our ready-to-fly plane will be using a CubeOrange autopilot and only requires a single line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:41
#: b11374bb669c4c179b2e5d1e7f42f45c
msgid "The firmware name can be customized by adding one line to the ``hwdef.dat`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:47
#: 533f652d876a4d559f19170c5cc09b10
msgid "Custom frame type strings can be created through Lua the scripting method ``motors:set_frame_string(\"Custom frame name\")``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:49
#: dd013a4343234a54b9aec75038133948
msgid "Now in that same directory, copy the base board's ``hwdef-bl.dat`` bootloader file, and then include a file named ``defaults.parm``. This file will be the parameter overrides of the standard defaults to match your system's configuration. Things like output function assignments, auxiliary RC switches, flight and tuning parameters, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:51
#: 572884ff2a504f43acec5cbd91bc5140
msgid "a parameter can be made readonly (ie user cannot change its value) by marking it ``@READONLY`` in the file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:53
#: 4721bad5074441649f64934569f14af9
msgid "The ``defaults.parm`` file should be as small as possible. Some boards only allow 1024 bytes total for this file. Every ASCII byte in the file counts against this limit (except for comment lines). Use integer values where possible. Below is a simple example. Serial port protocols,baud rate,and options defaults can be set directly in the hwdef, as well as NTF_LED_TYPES, and battery monitor defaults, and should be done there instead of a defaults file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:61
#: 4d2b6b4da33643a7868952ba6790f268
msgid "You can also embed :ref:`Lua scripts<common-lua-scripts>` in the ROM of the chip that will automatically run. Since Lua is currently only run on autopilots with a lot of flash space, they are only restricted in total aggregate size to available free flash memory. Put the scripts in a sub-directory called ``scripts``, i.e. ``libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/OEM_CubeOrange/scripts``. Files must end in ``.lua``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:63
#: 255f1e0005c6460aa06293a069dc5c2e
msgid "Alternatively, you can specify the LUA applet or driver at compile by using the \"--embed-<filename> command, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:69
#: adf946ccf577414ba1b8bd1088aab8af
msgid "The user may also run Lua scripts off the SD card, so care should be taken in naming the embedded script file names to not conflict with potential user file names. It is recommended that the file names of embedded Lua scripts be provided in the product documentation for the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:71
#: c7960e0cf8494532ae8c3ca3af9bc31f
msgid "You can also embed small pieces of documentation in the ROM of the chip that are readable when examining the @ROMFS folder via MAVFtp. These can be pictures or small informational documents. These must fit within the free flash space of the autopilot. These files can be located in sub-directories in ``libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/OEM_CubeOrange`` (e.g. ``libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/OEM_CubeOrange/AircraftManual``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:73
#: 899f51b2c6a74458aba56cde1302c004
msgid "Now build as normal with OEM-CubeOrange as the board name in the configuration. The default parameters, Lua scripts, and the custom firmware name will be embedded appropriately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:76
#: a0e178c668534a93b098f5ba67496d59
msgid "Alternative To Customizing hwdef.dat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-oem-customizations.rst:78
#: 063ab02f7a2e4ffcb7c536dd856799e3
msgid "Instead of creating a separate branch and modifying the hwdef file, you can also insert Lua scripts or even informational files into the ROMFS of the build. Simply go to the top level of your ArduPilot git checkout and create a sub-folder named \"ROMFS_custom\" in the root of the source tree. Place your LUA scripts in a sub-folder in this directory, named \"scripts\" (i.e. the path ``ardupilot/ROMFS_custom/scripts``). You can have other sub-folders for informational files and these will be included and viewable when examining the @ROMFS folder with MAVFtp."
msgstr ""
